\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A real volume for a conjugate pair}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Real fields tie a nonreal Fourier component to its complex conjugate. A real alternating form on the resulting rotation plane can have either sign on a fixed oriented orthonormal frame. How do the rotation planes and the genuinely real character spaces contribute to its [Pfaffian](fdip-008I)?}
